{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "wall-with-math",
  "title": "Wall — one Math Engine, band, poché and prism",
  "category": "Building",
  "object": {
    "hostKind": "segment",
    "name": "Wall",
    "symbol": "wall"
  },
  "description": "Wall — parameters and metrics for a canvas wall segment. It draws NOTHING itself: the canvas owns both\nthe 2D band (mitred union + poché hatch, set on the Network row or in Segment Properties → Display) and\nthe 3D extrusion, because only the canvas can see the mitred polygon that makes corners join. This object\nwould have to guess a plain rectangle from its two host points, which fought the canvas solid at every\njunction.\n\nWhat it does own: Thickness and Display mode stay in sync with the segment in both directions, Height\ndrives the segment's 3D extrusion, and the Math Engine publishes 15 metrics (length, plan area, volume,\nface / end / exposed area, bearing, elevations) for the Output block.\n\nRe-enable any Render 2D / 3D row to have the object draw again — the geometry is still computed.",
